                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Terrible game with some really great designs and music. \n\nPlaying it feels really really really really bad! \nOn a technical level, it's also really bad. \nEvery time I give Overture a chance, it puts me in an awful mood and I regret ever even looking at it at all.\n\nThe story is really integral to Guilty Gear (a funny wrinkle, for a game where Daisuke temporarily only had the rights to Sol and Ky - Dizzy features in the story, but is only ever referred to as the \"Maiden of the Grove\"), but the translation is really stilted and incoherent, and the voice direction isn't much better. I don't know. Watch a playthrough online or something. \n\nThis is honestly a curio at best. A pretty cool curio with a fully-featured Dustloop page. It goes on sale for four dollars. Make that call yourself.\n\nI thought I brought the right mindset to enjoy it despite (or for) its many quirks and problems, but I was wrong about that, and I've been wrong about it every time I returned to give it another go... maybe it's for you, but probably not.",
